{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-94a5aa3decbeb81b", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Neural Codec Language Models are Zero-Shot Text to Speech Synthesizers\narXiv: 2301.02111\nAuthors: Chengyi Wang, Sanyuan Chen, Yu Wu, Ziqiang Zhang, Long Zhou, Shujie Liu, Zhuo Chen, Yanqing Liu, Huaming Wang, Jinyu Li, Lei He, Sheng Zhao, Furu Wei\nYear: 2023 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose VALL-E, the first TTS framework with strong in-context learning capabilities, which treats TTS as a language model task using audio codec codes instead of traditional mel spectrograms.\n  2. We build a generalized TTS system by leveraging 60K hours of semi-supervised data, demonstrating that simply scaling up data has been underestimated for TTS.\n  3. VALL-E provides diverse outputs for the same input text and preserves the acoustic environment and speaker's emotion from the acoustic prompt.\n  4. We verify that VALL-E significantly outperforms the state-of-the-art zero-shot TTS system on LibriSpeech and VCTK in terms of speech naturalness and speaker similarity.\n\nTags: TTS, 压缩, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/功能-多说话人, 压缩/量化-RVQ", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "82477f26-2fd9-40b9-a72a-0d587552c79f", "uuid": "e541dd5d-7a30-4e4a-9fa2-8dd65215197e", "timestamp": "2026-07-29T07:37:57.738Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# Neural Codec Language Models are Zero-Shot Text to Speech Synthesizers\narXiv: 2301.02111\nAuthors: Chengyi Wang, Sanyuan Chen, Yu Wu, Ziqiang Zhang, Long Zhou, Shujie Liu, Zhuo Chen, Yanqing Liu, Huaming Wang, Jinyu Li, Lei He, Sheng Zhao, Furu Wei\nYear: 2023 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose VALL-E, the first TTS framework with strong in-context learning capabilities, which treats TTS as a language model task using audio codec codes instead of traditional mel spectrograms.\n  2. We build a generalized TTS system by leveraging 60K hours of semi-supervised data, demonstrating that simply scaling up data has been underestimated for TTS.\n  3. VALL-E provides diverse outputs for the same input text and preserves the acoustic environment and speaker's emotion from the acoustic prompt.\n  4. We verify that VALL-E significantly outperforms the state-of-the-art zero-shot TTS system on LibriSpeech and VCTK in terms of speech naturalness and speaker similarity.\n\nTags: TTS, 压缩, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/功能-多说话人, 压缩/量化-RVQ", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
