{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-8f93c8bea28ff08f", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# CosyVoice: A Scalable Multilingual Zero-shot Text-to-speech Synthesizer based on Supervised Semantic Tokens\narXiv: 2407.05407\nAuthors: Zhihao Du, Qian Chen, Shiliang Zhang, Kai Hu, Heng Lu, Yexin Yang, Hangrui Hu, Siqi Zheng, Yue Gu, Ziyang Ma, Zhifu Gao, Zhijie Yan\nYear: 2024 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We are the first to integrate supervised speech tokens into text-to-speech models, enhancing content consistency and speaker similarity in zero-shot voice cloning.\n  2. We propose CosyVoice, a scalable zero-shot TTS synthesis system that combines an LLM for text-to-token generation with a conditional flow matching model for token-to-speech synthesis, forsaking the need for additional phonemizers and forced aligners.\n  3. We refine the quality of generated speech by incorporating the x-vector into the LLM to separate speech modeling into semantic, speaker, and prosody components, and optimize the flow matching process with classifier-free guidance, a cosine scheduler, and masked conditions.\n\nTags: TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/功能-多语言, TTS/功能-多说话人, 压缩/监督-有监督, 压缩/语义声学-语义", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "82477f26-2fd9-40b9-a72a-0d587552c79f", "uuid": "8e63e89a-d827-4491-9638-540f002ed463", "timestamp": "2026-07-29T07:39:20.938Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# CosyVoice: A Scalable Multilingual Zero-shot Text-to-speech Synthesizer based on Supervised Semantic Tokens\narXiv: 2407.05407\nAuthors: Zhihao Du, Qian Chen, Shiliang Zhang, Kai Hu, Heng Lu, Yexin Yang, Hangrui Hu, Siqi Zheng, Yue Gu, Ziyang Ma, Zhifu Gao, Zhijie Yan\nYear: 2024 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We are the first to integrate supervised speech tokens into text-to-speech models, enhancing content consistency and speaker similarity in zero-shot voice cloning.\n  2. We propose CosyVoice, a scalable zero-shot TTS synthesis system that combines an LLM for text-to-token generation with a conditional flow matching model for token-to-speech synthesis, forsaking the need for additional phonemizers and forced aligners.\n  3. We refine the quality of generated speech by incorporating the x-vector into the LLM to separate speech modeling into semantic, speaker, and prosody components, and optimize the flow matching process with classifier-free guidance, a cosine scheduler, and masked conditions.\n\nTags: TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/功能-多语言, TTS/功能-多说话人, 压缩/监督-有监督, 压缩/语义声学-语义", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-92c7bf082ef84fbb", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# WavLM: Large-Scale Self-Supervised Pre-Training for Full Stack Speech Processing\narXiv: 2110.13900\nAuthors: Sanyuan Chen, Chengyi Wang, Zhengyang Chen, Yu Wu, Shujie Liu, Zhuo Chen, Jinyu Li, Naoyuki Kanda, Takuya Yoshioka, Xiong Xiao, Jian Wu, Long Zhou, Shuo Ren, Yanmin Qian, Yao Qian, Jian Wu, Michael Zeng, Xiangzhan Yu, Furu Wei\nYear: 2021 | Venue: \nTopic: speech_representation\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. WavLM introduces a general pre-trained model for full stack speech processing tasks, moving beyond the focus on specific task groups like ASR in prior self-supervised learning works.\n  2. A masked speech denoising and prediction framework is proposed to jointly learn speech content modeling and denoising, effectively improving performance on non-ASR tasks such as speaker verification, diarization, and separation.\n  3. Gated relative position bias is integrated into the Transformer structure to adaptively adjust relative position biases based on current speech content, enhancing sequence ordering capture and ASR performance.\n  4. The self-supervised speech pre-training data is scaled up to 94k hours from diverse domains, alleviating audiobook data bias and improving model robustness.\n  5. State-of-the-art results are achieved on the SUPERB benchmark and representative benchmarks for speaker verification, speech separation, and speaker diarization, with models and code publicly released.\n\nTags: SSL, ASR, SSL/预测式-离散", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "82477f26-2fd9-40b9-a72a-0d587552c79f", "uuid": "400db32d-789e-445a-b70a-37972f3a0946", "timestamp": "2026-07-29T07:39:21.275Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# WavLM: Large-Scale Self-Supervised Pre-Training for Full Stack Speech Processing\narXiv: 2110.13900\nAuthors: Sanyuan Chen, Chengyi Wang, Zhengyang Chen, Yu Wu, Shujie Liu, Zhuo Chen, Jinyu Li, Naoyuki Kanda, Takuya Yoshioka, Xiong Xiao, Jian Wu, Long Zhou, Shuo Ren, Yanmin Qian, Yao Qian, Jian Wu, Michael Zeng, Xiangzhan Yu, Furu Wei\nYear: 2021 | Venue: \nTopic: speech_representation\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. WavLM introduces a general pre-trained model for full stack speech processing tasks, moving beyond the focus on specific task groups like ASR in prior self-supervised learning works.\n  2. A masked speech denoising and prediction framework is proposed to jointly learn speech content modeling and denoising, effectively improving performance on non-ASR tasks such as speaker verification, diarization, and separation.\n  3. Gated relative position bias is integrated into the Transformer structure to adaptively adjust relative position biases based on current speech content, enhancing sequence ordering capture and ASR performance.\n  4. The self-supervised speech pre-training data is scaled up to 94k hours from diverse domains, alleviating audiobook data bias and improving model robustness.\n  5. State-of-the-art results are achieved on the SUPERB benchmark and representative benchmarks for speaker verification, speech separation, and speaker diarization, with models and code publicly released.\n\nTags: SSL, ASR, SSL/预测式-离散", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
